    <h1>About Drill Chart</h1>
    <p>This is a size reference for people standing in front of a drill index. Numbered, letter, fractional, and metric bits overlap. Tap drills are smaller than the screw. Clearance holes are larger. The pages keep those three jobs apart.</p>
    <p>Diameters follow common ASME B94.11M jobber charts. Tap drills are the usual 75% thread shop sizes. See <a href="/sources/">sources</a>.</p>
